clash-kde (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Status page lists live connections and can close them.
  * A speed test downloads through the proxy and directly at the same time. The size is set on the Other page.
  * Profiles lists proxy providers beside the profile list.
  * Own rules are edited as a draft and can be filled from a spreadsheet. A subscribed route or profile rule can be restored.

 -- KangxiDictionary <108598928+KangxiDictionary@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0800

clash-kde (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Status page can hide its note about the included panel widget.
  * Default discards unsaved route, profile, and selection edits.
  * The widget route menu no longer collapses while delays are updating.
  * A route can be edited beside the list, and the lists sort and search in place.
  * This account can open its mixed port to the LAN, and copying an address is a right-click.
  * Numbers and dates follow the desktop format. Compact mode applies with the rest of the draft.

 -- KangxiDictionary <108598928+KangxiDictionary@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:45:00 +0800

clash-kde (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Closing the system proxy also turns off the GNOME proxy.
  * The exit check follows the live path, and the address can be blurred.

